# gl11_state_probe64.expected - output of gl11_state_probe.c (x86_64 build) run on winoracle.
# Oracle: Windows 11 10.0.26200, Microsoft "GDI Generic" OpenGL 1.1.0 (glgetstring-GL_VENDOR / -GL_RENDERER / -GL_VERSION).
# The i686 build gives identical output except pointer-size in the setup line.
# Context: window-DC pixel format 3 (double-buffered RGBA, 32-bit colour, 32 depth bits, 8 stencil, 0 alpha), 320x200 client,
# first make-current. Every value below is the INITIAL value (the dump runs before any state-changing call).
# get-<NAME> lines: spec_n = value count in the OpenGL 1.1 state table, n = elements actually written. n == spec_n for all
# 238 pnames and none records an error. '# Table:' lines name the OpenGL 1.1 specification chapter 6 state table.
# Notable measured values (cite the tags):
#   get-GL_VIEWPORT 0 0 320 200 and get-GL_SCISSOR_BOX 0 0 320 200 (whole client area).
#   get-GL_CURRENT_INDEX 1, get-GL_CURRENT_RASTER_POSITION_VALID 1, get-GL_CURRENT_COLOR 1 1 1 1,
#   get-GL_CURRENT_NORMAL 0 0 1, get-GL_MATRIX_MODE 5888 (GL_MODELVIEW).
#   get-GL_MAX_MODELVIEW_STACK_DEPTH 32, GL_MAX_PROJECTION_STACK_DEPTH 10, GL_MAX_TEXTURE_STACK_DEPTH 10,
#   GL_MAX_ATTRIB_STACK_DEPTH 16, GL_MAX_CLIENT_ATTRIB_STACK_DEPTH 16, GL_MAX_NAME_STACK_DEPTH 128,
#   GL_MAX_LIST_NESTING 64, GL_MAX_EVAL_ORDER 30, GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE 1024, GL_MAX_LIGHTS 8, GL_MAX_CLIP_PLANES 6,
#   GL_MAX_PIXEL_MAP_TABLE 65536, GL_MAX_VIEWPORT_DIMS 16384 16384, GL_SUBPIXEL_BITS 3,
#   GL_POINT_SIZE_RANGE / GL_LINE_WIDTH_RANGE 0.5 10, granularity 0.125.
#   The stack-overflow lines show the depth reached: err-overflow-glPushMatrix-modelview ok-pushes=31 depth-after=32
#   (the stack holds 32 entries including the base), projection / texture 9 pushes (depth 10), glPushAttrib /
#   glPushClientAttrib 16 pushes (depth 16, so the 17th errors), glPushName 128 pushes (depth 128, select mode only).
# Error behaviour (err-* lines: first glGetError after the call, then what the second glGetError returns):
#   only the FIRST error is kept until read (err-two-errors-sequence: INVALID_VALUE then INVALID_ENUM reads
#   0x0501, 0, 0).
#   glGetError inside glBegin returns GL_INVALID_OPERATION and does NOT clear it, and the glBegin block still
#   closes: err-geterror-in-glBegin in-begin=0x0502 in-begin-again=0x0502 after-glEnd=0x0502 then=0.
#   Invalid-enum pnames (get-invalid-*): INVALID_ENUM and no elements written, for glGet*v and glIsEnabled;
#   GL 1.2+ pnames (GL_MAX_3D_TEXTURE_SIZE, GL_ALIASED_LINE_WIDTH_RANGE, GL_TEXTURE_BINDING_3D, GL_MAX_TEXTURE_UNITS)
#   are INVALID_ENUM. glGetString with a bad name: NULL + INVALID_ENUM.
#   Silent (no error) cases worth knowing: glEnableClientState(0x1234) (err-bad-cap-glEnableClientState),
#   glPushAttrib(0x80000000), glPushName/glPopName/glLoadName outside select mode, glCallList of an undefined list,
#   glGenLists(0), glAccum with no accumulation buffer, glEvalMesh2 with a bad mode, glArrayElement(-1),
#   glIndexPointer(GL_FLOAT,...), glGenLists/glDeleteLists inside glNewList, glGetIntegerv inside glNewList.
#   glClear(0x1) (an unknown bit) is INVALID_VALUE (err-bad-bits-glClear); glLineWidth(0) and glPointSize(0) are
#   INVALID_VALUE; glTexImage2D with 5 components is INVALID_ENUM; non-power-of-two width is INVALID_VALUE.
#   Calls inside glBegin that must fail with INVALID_OPERATION: glBegin, glEnable, glMatrixMode, glViewport,
#   glClear, glGenTextures, glGetIntegerv, glNewList, glPushMatrix. Allowed: glColor*, glNormal*, glTexCoord*,
#   glVertex*. glVertex outside glBegin: no error.
# gluErrorString (glu-error-* lines): "no error", "invalid enumerant" (GL_INVALID_ENUM and GLU_INVALID_ENUM),
#   "invalid value" (GL_INVALID_VALUE and GLU_INVALID_VALUE), "invalid operation", "stack overflow",
#   "stack underflow", "out of memory" (GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY and GLU_OUT_OF_MEMORY); GLU_INCOMPATIBLE_GL_VERSION,
#   GLU_INVALID_OPERATION and unknown codes return NULL. glu-getstring: GLU_VERSION "1.2.2.0 Microsoft Corporation",
#   GLU_EXTENSIONS "GL_EXT_bgra".
# glGetString(GL_EXTENSIONS) = "GL_WIN_swap_hint GL_EXT_bgra GL_EXT_paletted_texture"; GL_VERSION "1.1.0".
# Task 10 fix round 1 (re-run 2026-10-27, both builds identical apart from pointer-size): every earlier line is
#   unchanged; added copyteximage-/teximage-bad-internalformat-* (an unknown enum, 0, 5, GL_RED, GL_COLOR_INDEX and
#   1-4, 1D and 2D: all INVALID_ENUM except glTexImage with 1-4; checked before the size), texsubimage*/
#   copytexsubimage*-undefined-level (INVALID_VALUE from the region check; a 0x0 region of an undefined level is
#   INVALID_OPERATION), and aretexturesresident-* / texparam-resident-* (resident once level 0 holds client data:
#   TRUE after glTexImage2D with data, FALSE with a NULL pointer or no image; residences are written in order up
#   to the first name that is not an object, which stops with INVALID_VALUE).
# Task 11 (re-run 2026-10-27, both builds identical apart from pointer-size): every earlier line is unchanged;
#   added the "Raster position, glBitmap, glDrawPixels, glCopyPixels, glReadPixels" block (rasterpos-*, bitmap-*,
#   drawpixels-*, copypixels-*, readpixels-*). Raster x/y are quantised by GDI Generic to a fixed-point grid with a
#   small bias (10.25 -> 10.2539062); GL_CURRENT_RASTER_DISTANCE is the signed eye z (dist=-12 at eye (3,4,-12),
#   0.5 at eye z +0.5); a culled raster position clears only the valid bit (position, distance, colour and texture
#   coordinates keep the last valid values) and glBitmap then neither draws nor moves it; glReadPixels leaves the
#   client bytes of pixels outside the window untouched (0xab sentinel). Every GDI Generic pixel format has depth
#   and stencil buffers (pf-list), so the missing-buffer errors cannot be measured here.
# Task 12 (re-run 2026-10-27, both builds identical apart from pointer-size): every earlier line is unchanged;
#   added the "Display lists" block (list-*), run on a fresh context made current on the same DC. glGenLists is first
#   fit from 1 and ignores the list being compiled (it is not a name until glEndList); GL_LIST_INDEX is 0 outside
#   glNewList, GL_LIST_MODE keeps the last mode. glCallList(0) is INVALID_VALUE (also when compiled, at execution);
#   an offset that reaches list 0 in glCallLists is silently skipped. glNewList checks glBegin, then the mode
#   (INVALID_ENUM), then an open list (INVALID_OPERATION), then n = 0. glCallLists checks n < 0, then n = 0 (no
#   error even with a bad type), then the type. Errors of compiled commands appear when they execute (at compile
#   time only for COMPILE_AND_EXECUTE). The nesting limit executes 64 levels counting the outermost glCallList.
#   GL_FLOAT offsets are FLOORED (-0.25 -> -1), not truncated as the 1.1 text says. glPixelStore inside a
#   GL_COMPILE list is batched by opengl32: it takes effect only when a later command flushes the batch before
#   glEndList (list-not-compiled-pixelstore vs list-pixelstore-compile); Vitreo follows the spec (executed at once).
# Task 13 (re-run 2026-10-27): every earlier line is unchanged; added the GLU blocks after glu-error-* (glu_probe()).
#   The i686 build differs from this one only in pointer-size and glu-perspective-fovy180 (x87 cos/sin: m00
#   6.1230317691118863e-17 there, 6.1232342629258393e-17 here). GDI Generic stores matrices as floats, so every
#   glu-*-matrix value is float-rounded (glu-lookat-123-000-010 m[12] 5.96e-08, not 0).
#   Strings: tessellator (100151-100156) and NURBS (100251-100287) codes have strings, 100157/100158 are NULL
#   (gluErrorUnicodeStringEXT returns a non-NULL garbage pointer for those two: glu-errorw-0x1873D/E); every wide
#   string equals the ANSI one; pointers are stable.
#   Matrices: gluPerspective does nothing for aspect 0, zNear == zFar or sin(fovy/2) == 0; gluOrtho2D(l == r) is
#   glOrtho's INVALID_VALUE; gluPickMatrix does nothing for width/height <= 0; a degenerate gluLookAt leaves zero
#   rows (normalising a zero vector keeps it); GLU's GL calls are compiled into an open list and refused inside glBegin.
#   gluScaleImage: zero sizes -> 0 and nothing written, then negative -> GLU_INVALID_VALUE, then format/type ->
#   GLU_INVALID_ENUM; inside glBegin or with no current context (the pixel-store queries fail) -> 1285
#   (GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY), nothing written. Components go through 16 bits (ubyte *257, byte *516, short *2, ushort,
#   int >>15, uint >>16, float *65535 truncated; back: ubyte >>8, byte >>9, short >>1, uint *65537, int *65537>>1,
#   float /65535); colour-index formats keep raw values. An exact 2:1 shrink averages 2x2 with +2 rounding, any
#   other size is a box filter over [x-c/2, x+c/2) (or [x-0.5, x+0.5) when magnifying) that wraps around the image
#   edge and truncates. GL_BITMAP: bits -> 0/65535 (index formats 0/1); out bit = value > 32767 (index: value & 1);
#   unwritten bits of an output byte are kept.
#   gluBuild{1,2}DMipmaps: sizes go to the nearest power of two (3->4, 5->4, 6->8, 10->8, 12->16), clamped to
#   GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE (2000 -> 1024), then halve to 1x1; width/height < 1 -> GLU_INVALID_VALUE, then bad format/type
#   or STENCIL_INDEX/DEPTH_COMPONENT -> GLU_INVALID_ENUM; target/components errors are glTexImage's (ret 0); the
#   UNPACK_* modes are honoured for the source and restored; compiled into an open list.
#   Quadrics: errors go only to the GLU_ERROR callback (no GL error); slices < 2, stacks/loops < 1, negative radii or
#   height, outer < inner -> GLU_INVALID_VALUE; bad enums -> GLU_INVALID_ENUM (old value kept); gluQuadricTexture
#   takes any GLboolean. Slices (and sphere stacks) are capped at 239. glu-fb-* lines are GL_4D_COLOR_TEXTURE
#   feedback converted back to object space: x y z, then the normal (two lit passes), then s t. The error callback,
#   gluProject and the strings work with no current context (glu-noctx-*).
# Task 13 fix round 1 (re-run 2026-10-27): every earlier line is unchanged; added ext_probe() (ext-* lines) after the
#   GLU blocks. The two builds are again identical apart from pointer-size and glu-perspective-fovy180.
#   wglGetProcAddress (ext-gpa): non-NULL for glAddSwapHintRectWIN, glColorTableEXT, glColorSubTableEXT,
#   glGetColorTableEXT, glGetColorTableParameterivEXT, glGetColorTableParameterfvEXT and glDrawRangeElementsWIN;
#   NULL (ERROR_PROC_NOT_FOUND) for the other names tried; wglGetDefaultProcAddress returns the same pointers
#   (ext-defproc). glDrawRangeElementsWIN (ext-dre-*) draws like glDrawElements (indices outside [start, end] are
#   still drawn); end < start and count < 0 are INVALID_VALUE, a bad mode or type INVALID_ENUM, inside glBegin
#   INVALID_OPERATION; it is compiled into display lists.
#   GL_EXT_bgra (ext-bgra-*): GL_BGR_EXT / GL_BGRA_EXT are pixel formats of glTexImage1D/2D, glTexSubImage, glDrawPixels,
#   glReadPixels and glGetTexImage (3 / 4 components, blue first); with GL_BITMAP glTexImage / glDrawPixels are
#   INVALID_ENUM and glReadPixels INVALID_OPERATION; as an internal format (glTexImage, glCopyTexImage) INVALID_ENUM.
#   GL_EXT_paletted_texture (ext-pal-*): each texture object (and target 1D/2D, and each proxy) has a table, initially
#   1 entry, format GL_RGBA, every component size 8 (LUMINANCE/INTENSITY size and unknown pnames INVALID_ENUM).
#   glColorTableEXT takes internal formats 3, 4, RGB, RGBA and the sized RGB/RGBA ones (stored as given; sizes stay 8;
#   all four components are kept whatever the internal format), not LUMINANCE/ALPHA/INTENSITY/BGRA/1 (INVALID_ENUM);
#   width a power of two (else INVALID_VALUE; 4096 and 65536 were accepted in a run that left GDI Generic unstable, so
#   they are not probed); source formats RGB/RGBA/BGR/BGRA/RED/GREEN/BLUE/ALPHA (not LUMINANCE, LUMINANCE_ALPHA,
#   COLOR_INDEX, GL_BITMAP: INVALID_ENUM); targets TEXTURE_1D/2D and the proxies (glGetColorTableEXT on a proxy and
#   glColorSubTableEXT on a proxy: INVALID_ENUM). glGetColorTableEXT packs RGBA/RGB/BGRA/BGR/RED/BLUE/ALPHA (not
#   LUMINANCE, LUMINANCE_ALPHA, COLOR_INDEX, BITMAP). glColorSubTableEXT: start + count > width is INVALID_VALUE (a
#   negative start or count is accepted and corrupts GDI Generic's heap: not probed). Index textures: internal formats
#   COLOR_INDEX1/2/4/8/12/16_EXT with GL_COLOR_INDEX data (other data: INVALID_OPERATION; GL_COLOR_INDEX itself and
#   0x80E8: INVALID_ENUM); GL_TEXTURE_COMPONENTS reports the internal format; GL_TEXTURE_INDEX_SIZE_EXT is INVALID_ENUM
#   (iv and fv); indices are kept in 8 bits for INDEX1-8 and 16 for INDEX16 (index offset applies); glGetTexImage
#   returns indices for GL_COLOR_INDEX and looks them up in the current table for colour formats; drawing looks
#   them up in the table current at the draw; glTexSubImage of colour data into an index texture is INVALID_ENUM;
#   glCopyTexImage with an index format INVALID_OPERATION. glColorTableEXT is compiled into display lists and refused
#   inside glBegin, as is glGetColorTableParameter.
#   GL_WIN_swap_hint's effect on SwapBuffers is measured by swap_hint_probe.c (a visible window).
#   gluUnProject (ext-unproject-*): glu32 inverts by elimination with a zero-pivot test, so exactly rank-deficient
#   integer matrices and inexact near-singular ones succeed with huge coordinates (m1-m3, m8) and only a zero pivot
#   (m9) fails.
# Task 13 fix round 2: the fix2_probe() block was added (gluProject / gluUnProject with two non-identity matrices); every earlier line is unchanged.
setup pixelformat=3 setpf=1 ctx=ok makecurrent=1 pointer-size=8 client=320x200
